.TH AVR\-REPO\-MIRROR\-DELETE 1 "" "avr 0.1.6" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-repo-mirror-delete \- Disable a repository's avrea-git mirror.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr repo mirror delete
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Disable a repository's avrea-git mirror.
.PP
Stops mirroring the repository. The mirror configuration is retained but inert, so re-creating the mirror restores it. Requires the organization admin role.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr repo mirror delete --repo acme/widgets
    avr repo mirror delete --repo acme/widgets --yes
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    enabled, full_name, placements, repository_id
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fITEXT\fR
Repository (org/repo or rep-xxx). Auto-detected from git remote if omitted.
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR, \fB\-y\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-repo-mirror (1),
.BR avr-repo-mirror-create (1),
.BR avr-repo-mirror-status (1)
